From 25d9c15ec250702b069fef880ac609891d29e666 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:24:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] [UPSTREAM] notifications: harden sinks per review (redirects,
 secrets, concurrency)

Hardening of the notification sinks (0001-0004) after the Antigravity review:

- BLOCKING: the notification HTTP client disables redirects
  (reqwest::redirect::Policy::none()). reqwest strips Authorization on a
  cross-origin 30x but NOT a custom credential header like X-Gotify-Key, so a
  redirecting proxy / captive portal could otherwise harvest the Gotify token.
  Credential header values are also marked sensitive. send_notification treats a
  3xx as a delivery failure (regression test).
- BLOCKING: an invalid header value (e.g. a stray newline in a credential) now
  FAILS CLOSED with NotificationError::InvalidHeader (naming the header, not the
  value) rather than being dropped and the request sent unauthenticated. A
  whitespace-only secret (trim().is_empty()) is treated as unset.
- Gotify token must go in gotify_token (X-Gotify-Key, redacted). gotify_base_url
  strips any query/fragment (and trailing slash) from gotify_url; get_config
  returns the normalized form, and set_config normalizes BOTH the incoming and
  stored gotify_url before resolving the token, so a ?token= cannot leak via the
  config API and a benign GET->POST round-trip does not drop gotify_token.
- Webhook payload timestamp is the notification's receipt time, not the retry
  time (NotificationStatus.event_time).
- Sinks are delivered concurrently per tick (JoinSet): a slow/hung sink no
  longer blocks delivery to healthy ones within a tick (cross-tick decoupling is
  a documented follow-up). A join error is logged, not swallowed.
- POST /api/test-notification sends to EVERY configured sink concurrently and
  reports per-sink results (succeeded and failed), applying ntfy_headers, using
  the redirect-disabled client.
- Tests: URL stripped from a transport error; fail-closed on an invalid header;
  3xx rejected without following; no subscriber-identifier fields in the webhook
  payload; LowBattery/Update header+priority maps; gotify_base_url; get_config
  gotify_url normalization; trailing-slash round-trip keeps gotify_token;
  test-notification requires a sink.
- Nitpicks: sink_urls.get(); Gotify in the sink comment; stale config comment;
  resolve_endpoint_secret_* / redacts_secrets test names; no p.body clone; log
  join errors.

Ref: Orbic-Rayhunter T-OR-045..049 (PR #16/#17 review follow-up).
Signed-off-by: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
